Create POST route (accept JSON input)

1. Update main.py

• Add this below your existing route:

  • from pydantic import BaseModel

  • class Item(BaseModel):
      • name: str
      • value: int

  • @app.post("/data")
  • def receive_data(item: Item):
      • return {"received": item}

2. Restart not needed
• Because you used --reload, changes auto-apply

3. Test it

• Open:
  • http://127.0.0.1:8000/docs

Then:
• Find /data
• Click “Try it out”
• Input:
  • {
      "name": "test",
      "value": 123
    }
• Click “Execute”

Expected output
• {
    "received": {
      "name": "test",
      "value": 123
    }
  }
